From c0c3dcbe73b5dcc4e8baee487581fda4fda67d6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:06:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: piano_mca: integrate authenticated FFC with
 recovery

Keep the factory FFC stages, gauge authentication, battery aging and PMIC
sharing alongside the existing ordinary recharge and fault state machine.
Use the six IIO temperatures and calibrated skin policy for both modes,
rather than registering another thermal zone or bypassing its budget.

Only change gauge modes after both charging paths are paused. Roll back
partial mode changes, retry an unconfirmed PMIC pause, preserve fault and
full votes, and keep the 4480 mV PMIC cutoff through source-budget changes.

Exercise the actual policy with the existing virtual supplies: both-gauge
authentication, FFC temperature and thermal limits, partial writes,
inhibition, full votes, aging, tail charge and stop confirmation retries.
